    <string name="call_abs_volume_caveat">An experiment. On some Samsung phones it leaves more headroom so calls can get louder, but it mostly changes how media volume behaves (you may need to turn up both sides for music) and the in-call effect isn\'t guaranteed. To revert, switch it back here, or in Developer options → “Disable absolute volume”, then reconnect.</string>
    <string name="call_honest_title">Your voice on calls</string>
    <string name="call_honest_body">No app can process the call microphone: on Android it goes from the headset to the modem or the calling app without passing through other apps, and this firmware has no mic EQ. What does help is a wideband call codec (mSBC or LC3) and LE Audio; if you still sound bad on mSBC or LC3, the limit is the network or the calling app. Self Voice (More → Sidetone) changes only what you hear.</string>

